      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:1:40:2",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا الْحَسَنِ الْأَوَّلَ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ النَّفَقَةِ عَلَى الْعِيَالِ فَقَالَ مَا بَيْنَ الْمَكْرُوهَيْنِ الْإِسْرَافِ وَ الْإِقْتَارِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "And from him, from his father, from Muhammad Bin Amro, from Abdullah Bin Aban who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> the 1<sup>st</sup>, about the spending upon the dependants. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘What is between the two (limits of) abhorrence – the extravagance and the miserliness’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. It is narrated from him (narrator of previous Hadith) from his father from Muhammad ibn ‘Ammar from ‘Abd Allah ibn Aban who has said the following: “Once I asked abu al-Hassan, the 1st, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the expenses of one’s dependents. He (the Imam) replied, ‘It is between the two detestable limits: namely, excessive spending and severe austerity.’” "
        ]
      }
